Title: Bug: test_telemetry_queue_buffer_cnt test does not account for a single BUFFER_QUEUE entry for an interface

Failure report:
### Is it platform specific

generic

### Importance or Severity

Critical

### Description of the bug

In some SKU's and config

BUFFER_QUEUE may have config such as

    "BUFFER_QUEUE": {
        "Ethernet0|0-2": {
            "profile": "egress_lossy_profile"
        },
        "Ethernet0|3-4": {
            "profile": "egress_lossless_profile"
        },
        "Ethernet0|5-7": {
            "profile": "egress_lossy_profile"
        },

or even

    "BUFFER_QUEUE": {
        "Ethernet0|0": {
            "profile": "egress_lossy_profile"
        },
        "Ethernet0|1": {
            "profile": "egress_lossless_profile"
        },
        "Ethernet0|2": {
            "profile": "egress_lossy_profile"
        },  ... etc

The test works fine for the above configs.

However if the BUFFER_QUEUE was configured such as

    "BUFFER_QUEUE": {
        "Ethernet0|0-9": {
            "profile": "egress_lossy_profile"
        },
        "Ethernet100|0-9": {
            "profile": "egress_lossless_profile"
        },
        "Ethernet200|0-9": {
            "profile": "egress_lossy_profile"
        },

When we delete Ethernet0|0-9 as part of del data['BUFFER_QUEUE'][ interface_buffer_queues[0] ] we end up deleting all queues for that interface from COUNTERS_QUEUE_NAME_MAP which causes check_buffer_queues_cnt_cmd_output to always return false.

### Steps to Reproduce

Run the test_telemetry_queue_buffer_cnt testcase on configurations that have only a single BUFFER_QUEUE entry for an interface that will be selected.

